<h2>Find an account</h2>
<% if @email_in_url %>
  <p class="degraded">Email lookups go through this form, not the URL: an address in a query string is written to
    browser history and to every access log between you and this process. The deep link from the colonel
    console carries an external id only.</p>
<% end %>
<form method="post" action="/account">
  <%== csrf_tag('/account') %>
  <label for="q">Email or external id</label>
  <input type="search" id="q" name="q" autocomplete="off">
  <input type="submit" value="Find">
</form>
<p class="footnote">Exact match only, on <code>email</code> first and then <code>external_id</code>. No prefixes, no
  wildcards: this is a jump box, not a search engine, and a prefix search is a way to page through the user table by
  guessing. A single match redirects to that account's page; an email held
  by more than one account (a closed account's address can be re-registered) offers the choice instead.</p>
